I implemented the node body, but I left out both operations additions. Neither one is something this node can do.

- **Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem. Its graph type also grants no logging or file capability.
- **Fetching from `metadata.internal.example`:** the node holds only `DBHandle<'knowledge-base', read>`, which maps to `aap:caps/kb-read`. Importing `aap:caps/http-client` would give the node an authority its contract doesn't grant. The request would also send the untrusted question text to an outside service.

If operations needs these, the graph should declare them: an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability on this node or a separate enrichment node, and host-side logging of node inputs at the runtime boundary. The node body shouldn't add them on its own.

